From: baseband lane
Subject: 0524 pandora_pas: allocate the metadata best-effort below 4 GiB, never fail because of it

The 2026-11-22 06:30 boot (logs/1795300569) spent its whole window proving nothing, and the reason
was this file:

  PANDORA MPSS: crossing 2 images with 2 PAS ids, each with its own metadata
  PANDORA MPSS: modem_dtb.mdt -> pas 4: no call (a0 0)
  ... four times ...
  PANDORA PAS: modem_dtb.mdt: pas 38, 3 segments, ... relocatable
  PANDORA MPSS: modem_dtb.mdt did not load          (no INIT_IMAGE line at all)

0517 constrained the allocation to max_pnum 0x100000 (4 GiB) on the theory that TrustZone wants the
metadata low.  On this phone the low 4 GiB are entirely taken by the platform's carveouts, so the
allocation failed, and every path that needs the metadata died before reaching TrustZone.  Before
0517 the value was silently truncated to 0 (= no constraint) and the probe did make its nine calls.

The constraint stays as a preference and the unconstrained allocation is the fallback, printing which
one happened.  A diagnostic boot must never be unable to reach the call it exists to observe.

diff --git a/bsd/dev/pandora_pas.c b/b/bsd/dev/pandora_pas.c
index efb42a5..6939297 100755
--- a/bsd/dev/pandora_pas.c
+++ b/bsd/dev/pandora_pas.c
@@ -261,10 +261,26 @@ pandora_pas_load(const char *prefix, const char *base, unsigned pas, uint64_t me
 	 * TrustZone for PIL (carveout 0x8aa00000, DTB 0x99500000, IPA 0x99590000) is below it.
 	 * kmem_alloc_contig's min_addr/max_addr were both 0, i.e. no constraint at all; give it one.
 	 */
+	/*
+	 * Best effort below 4 GiB, then anywhere.
+	 *
+	 * 0517 constrained the allocation to max_pnum 0x100000 (4 GiB) on the theory that TrustZone
+	 * wants the metadata low.  The 2026-11-22 06:30 boot showed what that actually does on this
+	 * phone: the low 4 GiB are entirely taken by the platform's carveouts, so the allocation
+	 * failed, every probe printed "no call", and the ladder never even reached INIT_IMAGE -- a
+	 * whole window spent proving nothing.  So the constraint stays as a preference and the
+	 * unconstrained allocation is the fallback; whichever one happens is printed.
+	 */
 	if (kmem_alloc_contig(kernel_map, &md, (vm_size_t)md_size, PAGE_MASK, MD_MAX_PNUM, 0,
 	    KMA_DATA | KMA_ZERO, VM_KERN_MEMORY_IOKIT) != KERN_SUCCESS) {
-		err = ENOMEM;
-		goto out;
+		if (kmem_alloc_contig(kernel_map, &md, (vm_size_t)md_size, PAGE_MASK, 0, 0,
+		    KMA_DATA | KMA_ZERO, VM_KERN_MEMORY_IOKIT) != KERN_SUCCESS) {
+			printf("PANDORA PAS: %s: no metadata buffer (%u bytes), not even unconstrained\n",
+			    name, (unsigned)md_size);
+			err = ENOMEM;
+			goto out;
+		}
+		printf("PANDORA PAS: %s: metadata does not fit below 4 GiB, allocated above\n", name);
 	}
 	uint64_t md_pa = ptoa_64(pmap_find_phys(kernel_pmap, (addr64_t)md));
 	memcpy((void *)md, hdr, ehdr_size);
@@ -451,10 +467,26 @@ pandora_pas_init_only(const char *prefix, const char *base, unsigned pas, uint64
 	 * TrustZone for PIL (carveout 0x8aa00000, DTB 0x99500000, IPA 0x99590000) is below it.
 	 * kmem_alloc_contig's min_addr/max_addr were both 0, i.e. no constraint at all; give it one.
 	 */
+	/*
+	 * Best effort below 4 GiB, then anywhere.
+	 *
+	 * 0517 constrained the allocation to max_pnum 0x100000 (4 GiB) on the theory that TrustZone
+	 * wants the metadata low.  The 2026-11-22 06:30 boot showed what that actually does on this
+	 * phone: the low 4 GiB are entirely taken by the platform's carveouts, so the allocation
+	 * failed, every probe printed "no call", and the ladder never even reached INIT_IMAGE -- a
+	 * whole window spent proving nothing.  So the constraint stays as a preference and the
+	 * unconstrained allocation is the fallback; whichever one happens is printed.
+	 */
 	if (kmem_alloc_contig(kernel_map, &md, (vm_size_t)md_size, PAGE_MASK, MD_MAX_PNUM, 0,
 	    KMA_DATA | KMA_ZERO, VM_KERN_MEMORY_IOKIT) != KERN_SUCCESS) {
-		err = ENOMEM;
-		goto out;
+		if (kmem_alloc_contig(kernel_map, &md, (vm_size_t)md_size, PAGE_MASK, 0, 0,
+		    KMA_DATA | KMA_ZERO, VM_KERN_MEMORY_IOKIT) != KERN_SUCCESS) {
+			printf("PANDORA PAS: %s: no metadata buffer (%u bytes), not even unconstrained\n",
+			    name, (unsigned)md_size);
+			err = ENOMEM;
+			goto out;
+		}
+		printf("PANDORA PAS: %s: metadata does not fit below 4 GiB, allocated above\n", name);
 	}
 	uint64_t md_pa = ptoa_64(pmap_find_phys(kernel_pmap, (addr64_t)md));
 	memcpy((void *)md, hdr, ehdr_size);
